votes.reasoning:
**Defect: off-by-one in the elevate branch.** The condition `if ( i >= p )` should be `if ( i > p )`.

- **The equal case does work it should skip.** When the requested degree already equals the current maximum degree (`i == p`), `setDegree` should do nothing. Instead it calls `degreeElevate(0)`.
- **The call can fail outright.** For any basis that does not override `degreeElevate`, the base `gsBasis<T>::degreeElevate` is `GISMO_NO_IMPLEMENTATION`. So a call meant to be a no-op throws. This affects every subclass that only implements reduction, or neither operation.
- **Overriding subclasses still do needless work.** Where `degreeElevate` is overridden, an elevation by 0 is not guaranteed to be free. Hierarchical and tensor bases may rebuild internal structures, invalidate caches, or hit `GISMO_ASSERT(i > 0)`-style checks in some implementations.
- **The bug shows in the redundant else branch.** After `i >= p`, the `else if ( i < p )` test is always true. A correct three-way split needs both branches to be strict (`i > p` and `i < p`), so `i == p` falls through and does nothing.

**Fix:**
```cpp
if ( i > p )
    degreeElevate(i - p);
else if ( i < p )
    degreeReduce(p - i);
```

